+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need to change JSON documents with standard patches. The toolkit implements published standards, and RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) is the standard way to express such changes; it builds on the RFC 6901 pointers the library already supports.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing RFC 6902 with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- It returns the patched document as a new value and never mutates its input (neither the document nor the patch).
+- It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid or when an operation fails, including a failed `test`. No partial result is returned.
+- Document the function in `README.md`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document without mutating it, with error reporting for invalid patches and failed operations.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New module `src/json-patch.ts`, new export in `src/index.ts`, new tests in `test/`, README section.
+- The pointer parsing of `src/json-pointer.ts` is reused (internal export only); the behaviour of `resolvePointer` is unchanged.
+- No new dependencies.
