+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+Apply RFC 6902 JSON Patches to JSON documents, returning a new document and rejecting invalid patches and failing operations with an error.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch application
+Applying a patch SHALL apply its operations in order, each to the result of the previous one, and SHALL return the resulting document as a new value. The input document and the patch SHALL NOT be mutated, and the result SHALL NOT share mutable structure with them. An empty patch SHALL return a copy of the document. If any operation fails, applying the patch SHALL throw an error and return nothing.
+
+#### Scenario: Operations in order
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"a":1}` and the patch is `[{"op":"add","path":"/b","value":2},{"op":"replace","path":"/b","value":3}]`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":1,"b":3}`
+
+#### Scenario: Input not mutated
+- **WHEN** any patch is applied to a document
+- **THEN** the document and the patch are unchanged afterwards, and later changes to the result do not affect them
+
+#### Scenario: Failure in the middle
+- **WHEN** the second operation of a patch fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the document is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: Patch validity
+A patch SHALL be an array of operation objects. Each operation SHALL have an `op` member that is one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` or `test`, and a `path` member that is a valid JSON Pointer string. `add`, `replace` and `test` SHALL have a `value` member (which may be `null`); `move` and `copy` SHALL have a `from` member that is a valid JSON Pointer string. Members not defined for an operation SHALL be ignored. Any other patch SHALL cause an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Patch not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object or any non-array value
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown or missing op
+- **WHEN** an operation has an unknown `op` (for example `"merge"`), no `op`, or a non-string `op`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid members
+- **WHEN** an operation lacks `path`, has an invalid pointer as `path` or `from`, lacks `value` where required, or lacks `from` for `move` or `copy`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value
+- **WHEN** the operation is `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":null}`
+- **THEN** it is valid and sets `a` to `null`
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid operation not reached
+- **WHEN** the first operation of a patch is valid and the second is invalid
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Add operation
+`add` SHALL set the value at `path`. The parent of the target SHALL exist. For an object parent, the member is added, or its value replaced if it exists. For an array parent, the value is inserted before the given index, shifting later elements; an index equal to the array length, or the token `-`, appends. An index greater than the length, or one that is not a valid array index, SHALL cause an error. With the empty `path`, the whole document is replaced by the value.
+
+#### Scenario: Add member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/b","value":2}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":1,"b":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace existing member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":2}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Insert into array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a/1","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["p","x","q"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Append to array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a/-","value":"x"}` or `{"op":"add","path":"/a/2","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["p","q","x"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Index out of range
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a/3","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"a":["p","q"]}`, or the index is malformed (`/a/01`, `/a/-1`, `/a/x`)
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing parent
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/x/y","value":1}` is applied to `{"a":1}`, or the parent is a scalar
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace whole document
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"","value":[1]}` is applied to any document
+- **THEN** the result is `[1]`
+
+### Requirement: Remove operation
+`remove` SHALL remove the value at `path`, which SHALL exist, otherwise an error is thrown. Removing an array element shifts later elements down. Removing the whole document (empty `path`) is not defined by the RFC for a result and SHALL cause an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/a"}` is applied to `{"a":1,"b":2}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/a/0"}` is applied to `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["q"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** the target member or element does not exist, including the `-` token
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Replace operation
+`replace` SHALL replace the value at `path` with `value`. The target SHALL exist, otherwise an error is thrown. With the empty `path`, the whole document is replaced.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member or element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/a/0","value":9}` is applied to `{"a":[1,2]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":[9,2]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/b","value":1}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Move operation
+`move` SHALL remove the value at `from` and add it at `path`, as `remove` then `add`. `from` SHALL exist. A `from` that is a proper prefix of `path` (moving a value into one of its own children) SHALL cause an error. Moving a value to its own location SHALL leave the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/a","path":"/b"}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move within an array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/a/0","path":"/a/2"}` is applied to `{"a":["p","q","r"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["q","r","p"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/a","path":"/a/b"}` is applied to `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move to itself
+- **WHEN** `from` and `path` are equal and exist
+- **THEN** the document is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: Copy operation
+`copy` SHALL add at `path` a deep copy of the value at `from`, as `add` does. `from` SHALL exist, otherwise an error is thrown. The copy SHALL NOT share structure with the original.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"copy","from":"/a","path":"/b"}` is applied to `{"a":{"x":1}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{"x":1},"b":{"x":1}}`, and a later operation changing `/b/x` leaves `/a/x` equal to `1`
+
+#### Scenario: Copy from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Test operation
+`test` SHALL succeed, leaving the document unchanged, when the value at `path` equals `value`, and SHALL cause an error otherwise, including when `path` does not exist. Equality is JSON equality: values of different types are unequal; numbers are equal when numerically equal; strings are equal when their characters are the same; arrays are equal when they have the same length and pairwise equal elements in order; objects are equal when they have the same set of member names and equal values for each, regardless of member order.
+
+#### Scenario: Equal values
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a","value":{"y":2,"x":1}}` is applied to `{"a":{"x":1,"y":2}}`
+- **THEN** the patch succeeds
+
+#### Scenario: Different values
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a","value":"1"}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing target
+- **WHEN** the `path` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test guards later operations
+- **WHEN** a failed `test` is followed by other operations
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and no result is returned
